1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,380
Myth or reality: your washing machine is cheap to run.

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:07,908
The machine itself uses about thirteen dollars of electricity a year.

3
00:00:08,028 --> 00:00:14,716
But Energy Star says about ninety percent of the energy it takes to run a washer goes into heating the water.

4
00:00:14,836 --> 00:00:20,503
And an electric water heater costs the average home about four hundred and ninety-two dollars a year.

5
00:00:20,623 --> 00:00:26,315
Switching from hot to warm can cut the washer's energy use in half. Cold saves even more.

6
00:00:26,435 --> 00:00:30,445
So, the verdict? Half true. The machine is cheap. The hot water is not.

7
00:00:30,565 --> 00:00:37,168
I ranked fifteen appliances by yearly cost, full video linked. So, is your washing machine cheap to run?
